# What updaters/040-asdf does with each asdf tool. One tool per line:
#
#   <tool> latest   install the newest release and make it the global version
#   <tool> stable   as latest, but hold back from a brand new minor series:
#                   if the newest release is x.y.0 or x.y.1, use the newest
#                   release of the series before it
#   <tool> remove   uninstall every version, remove the plugin and its line
#                   in ~/.tool-versions
#
# A tool that is not listed here is never touched. After a tool is updated,
# its older versions are uninstalled unless a project pins them (a
# .tool-versions, .nvmrc, .node-version or .python-version under ~/projects).

nodejs latest
python stable
direnv latest
ruby latest
rust latest
golang latest
terraform latest
dotnet latest
lua latest
make latest

deno remove
